      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "if the compatibility for the optimizer is added to a shader will it be a simple include cignic, that allows the shader to still function? \n\nI try to reuse the same functions and textures in weird ways to get funny effects working to avoid excessive compute expense but I would love to see how the system works. \n\nif it allows for abnormal function plugging such as running Udon video texture through a bunch of distortions, turbulent flow calculations, sampling basic edge detections for a starting point of a curve to use as a procedural normal to use for a  shading specular calculation as well as paralax mapped waveforms n such.. Basically will it be able to support the full range of HLSL that works on vrchat? ._.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
